# The standard `math` module: the checked conversions between the numeric types, and from the
# integer types to `rune`, as methods of the converted type. `n.toU8()` is `Some` of the same
# number as a `u8` when `n` has one, and `None` otherwise; a float's fraction is dropped, as
# `u8(f)` drops it. The conversions are generated (`math_conversions` in the compiler's
# `stdlib.rs`).
